# Guide films must be unique

When **creating** a guide or **changing its film list**, run both checks **before** writing or shipping titles. Do not pick first and verify later.

## 1. Not in our guides

Exact `films.title` (and Flow `anchorTitle`) must not appear in any other `lib/guides/*.mjs` article.

Same studio or director in another guide is allowed. The same title is not.

## 2. Not a regular guest of competing internet articles

Search competing **roundups for this article’s target queries** (8–30 film listicles: “non Disney animated movies”, “movies like Flow”, “weird animated movies”, etc.).

A title **fails** if it is a listed pick in **2+** such roundups.

Ignore: Wikipedia, a review of that one film, 100-film encyclopedias, generic “best animation of all time” unless that is the query.

## 3. Report, then replace

Before keeping a list, report both checks title by title. Replace every fail. Only then edit the guide.

Example: Spirited Away and Persepolis sit on most “non Disney” listicles — they fail check 2 even if they pass check 1.
